# ── Secrets — NEVER commit ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Real Telegram api_id/api_hash live here (partial class; see TelegArm/Core/ApiCredentials.cs).
# The committed template is ApiCredentials.Local.cs.example (placeholders only).
ApiCredentials.Local.cs

# ── Build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
.vs/
*.user
*.suo

# ── Native build residue ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# rlottie ships as a DLL only: the app loads it by P/Invoke ([DllImport], cdecl),
# so the linker's import library (.lib) and export file (.exp) are never used —
# not at build time, not at runtime. Only rlottie.dll is referenced by the csproj.
TelegArm/rlottie/**/*.lib
TelegArm/rlottie/**/*.exp

# ── Sensitive runtime / auth material (if it ever lands in-tree) ──────────
*.session
TelegArm.session
TelegArm.phone
settings.json
accounts/
Cache/

# ── Distributable app builds (compiled binary WITH embedded keys) — never commit ──
# NOTE: intentionally NOT "*.zip" — noto-emoji.zip / libvlc-*.zip are required build
# Content (see TelegArm.csproj) and must stay tracked for a clean clone to build.
TelegArm*.zip
installer/Output/
TelegArm-Setup-*.exe

# ── Dev scratch / captures (never belong in the repo) ─────────────────────
asyncvoid_report.txt
blindspots.txt
telegarm-debug.log
crash.log
*.ogg

# ── Tooling / packages ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
nuget.exe
packages/

# ── Internal docs + AI session memory (kept LOCAL — travels with the folder,
#    deliberately NOT published; see .claude/NOTES-carried.md) ─────────────
# Leading "/" = ROOT-ANCHORED, on purpose: a bare "BUILD.md" would also match
# third-party/rlottie/BUILD.md (exactly the trap described at the bottom of this file).
/mdfiles/
/.claude/
/CLAUDE.md
/BUILD.md
/STATE.md
/INVARIANTS.md

# ── DO NOT add unanchored asset names here ────────────────────────────────
# A bare pattern like "icon.ico" matches at EVERY depth, which silently excluded
# img-icon/{icon,trayicon,trayicon-unread}.ico + img-icon/TelegArm.png from the
# repo — while TelegArm.csproj REQUIRES them (<ApplicationIcon> + <Content>), so a
# fresh clone could not build. Anchor any future asset rule with a leading "/".
